                    insight_seat:           `Strategic seat earned: you turned data into a defensible decision — a narrow causal question, a cause-addressing intervention proven with a control group, manager adoption designed in, and an R$ ROI the CFO recognises. HR moved from cost to investment.`,
                    insight_correlation:    `ROI the CFO won't buy: your headline number may look positive, but with no measurement design — or a correlation pitch — she can't tell your program from the market or luck. Correlation isn't causation, and it isn't ROI.`,
                    insight_thin:           `You cleared the R$8M target, but the proof is thin. Without strong causal confidence and adoption the CFO may accept the number this cycle, yet the case is fragile and easily challenged next year.`,
                    insight_short:          `You fell short of the R$8M defensible ROI. The budget is cut 15% and reallocated, and HR loses its seat in the strategy conversation. Re-examine which lever you left unproven — most likely the question, the cause, or the measurement.`,
                    insight_diffuse:        `Diffuse spend: by splitting the frozen budget across several programs you recreated exactly what the CFO froze and can't prove any single lever worked. Focus is the condition for a provable ROI.`,
                    insight_bonus:          `You bought the symptom: across-the-board retention bonuses pause exits without fixing the bad-manager and over-utilisation drivers — so the CFO heavily discounts the attrition you claim to avoid.`,
                    insight_lowadoption:    `Adoption stayed low: line managers never bought in, so even a well-targeted intervention earned a fraction of its potential return. Adoption is part of the intervention's value, not a footnote.`,
                    insight_rightquestion:  `You asked the right question: by targeting the ~600 high performers on over-utilised projects under weak managers, every real you spent was aimed at the actual driver — the heart of analytics-led HR.`,

                    hint_correlation:       `You're claiming returns from a correlation with no design to isolate the effect. Fund a control group or staggered rollout, or the CFO will reject the ROI as coincidence.`,
                    hint_diffuse:           `You've spread the frozen budget across programs — now nothing is provable. Concentrate on one cause-addressing intervention plus a measurement design.`,
                    hint_adoption:          `Manager adoption is dangerously low. Make billability the ally and design buy-in, or even a perfect intervention earns near-zero in the real world.`,
